# Compiled artifacts of the C assembler. Regenerate with: cd mac-c && make
mac-c/*.o
mac-c/mac-as
mac-c/mac-as.exe
mac-c/test_mac
mac-c/test_mac.exe

# NOTE: Build/ is deliberately NOT ignored. It holds the assembler's output
# (ASYMB/BSYMB symbol dumps, LIST1-5 listings) and is kept in the repository
# so the result is browsable without running a build. It is still fully
# regenerable: cd mac-c && ./build_tss_assysa.sh

# Disposable nd100x bring-up / login-test disc images (multi-MB, regenerated by
# the bringup/ scripts and the ad-hoc login tests).
Build/bringup/
Build/coldstart_test/

# Transient outputs left in mac-c/ when a build script is run from that dir
# (the real, browsable copies live under Build/).
mac-c/DSYMB.SYMB
mac-c/LIST*.SYMB
mac-c/build.err
mac-c/build.out
